{"skill":{"slug":"humanizer-zh","displayName":"humanizer-zh"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770692774916,"changelog":"humanizer-zh 1.0.0 发布说明\n\n- 首次发布中文“去除 AI 写作痕迹”技能，基于维基百科和相关 AI 文本识别社区指南。\n- 明确列出 24 种常见 AI 写作模式及具体示例，包括夸大语言、三段式、AI 词汇、模糊归因等。\n- 详细提供针对每种模式的改写方法及前后对比，附带内容与语言风格的操作建议。\n- 补充“注入灵魂”写作指导，强调人性化表达和节奏变化。\n- 内置编辑流程、快速检查清单和 50 分制质量评分标准，用于自查与复评。","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":7799,"sha256":"60cd3ed8b4753837ca8f8fcebf6076a38591a269d91ea1791aa7448e5a1b1b58","contentType":"text/x-markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":18898,"sha256":"e0edbdbc9008644263d5573fb59beac95794e188fd99c35012bfd79e9ae4beeb","contentType":"text/x-markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2154,"sha256":"ea6d5a1102198eabc00f4adf588f1fa3e904b4c89fb57baa51957ac21f5f1798","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789057133300,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"6bfd0d13ae3dacd5b9ef3483867c2d105e84aa09914aff62ebe5bb5f7963930a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/6bfd0d13ae3dacd5b9ef3483867c2d105e84aa09914aff62ebe5bb5f7963930a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: humanizer-zh\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw skill 'humanizer-zh' is classified as benign. While it requests broad file system permissions (`Read`, `Write`, `Edit`) in `SKILL.md`, these are plausibly needed for its stated purpose of processing and humanizing text, including content from files, as demonstrated in the `README.md` usage examples. Crucially, the `SKILL.md` instructions, which guide the AI agent, are entirely focused on text analysis and rewriting, containing no evidence of prompt injection, data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or any other intentional harmful behavior.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162662092},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":26,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789057133300},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill itself is a coherent Chinese text-editing guide, but its recommended unpinned npx install path creates avoidable supply-chain risk.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Read, Write, Edit, and AskUserQuestion are proportionate for a skill that can rewrite pasted text or user-selected files, but users should invoke it only on content they intend to modify.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"README.md recommends `npx skills add https://github.com/op7418/Humanizer-zh.git` without pinning the npm package, repository commit, or file hashes, so installation can execute mutable remote installer code not represented by the reviewed Markdown artifacts.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The trigger is somewhat broad for general editing/review requests, and the skill is strongly Chinese-oriented; this may cause unwanted style or language changes, but it is not evidence of malicious behavior.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact shows no background workers, credential access, memory poisoning, or persistence beyond normal skill installation, but the unpinned installer could place changed skill content if the remote source changes.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The runtime instructions match the stated purpose: identify AI-like writing patterns and rewrite text more naturally while preserving meaning and tone.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only after reviewing the source you are actually installing. Prefer the manual or git-clone path pinned to a trusted commit instead of the recommended unpinned npx command, and use the skill only on text or files you are comfortable having rewritten.","findings":"[RP1] unexpected: Accepted as a material install concern: the recommended npx command is not pinned or hash-verified and is unnecessary for a Markdown-only skill.\n[T08] unexpected: Consistent with the install concern above; no malicious payload was found in the reviewed files, but the documented installation path crosses an unsafe trust boundary.\n[SQP-1] expected: Downgraded to a usability/scoping note: broad editing triggers could cause unwanted rewrites, but the behavior is aligned with the skill's text-humanizing purpose.\n[SQP-3] expected: Downgraded: the skill name, README, and examples clearly indicate a Chinese version, though users working in other languages should avoid accidental activation.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789057133300}}}}}